{"text":"{
  "status": "NEEDS_IMPROVEMENT",
  "core_findings": [
    "Electronics has the weakest sampled separation: its 10th-percentile margin is 0.0265, negatives outrank positives at 9.7% of positions, and 14.82% have margins below 0.5.",
    "The other datasets show stronger separation, especially CDs_and_Vinyl. Embedding similarity scores of 0.5057–0.515 correspond to mean cosine similarities near zero, providing no evidence of broad directional collapse."
  ],
  "key_implications": [
    "Electronics has the largest proportion of confusing positive-negative comparisons in these diagnostics.",
    "Item embeddings remain directionally varied across all four datasets.",
    "These sampled margins alone do not establish validation HR@10 or generalization quality."
  ],
  "evidence": {
    "headline_metrics": {
      "Electronics:pos_neg_margin_p10": 0.0265,
      "Electronics:pos_neg_neg_beats_pos_rate": 0.097,
      "Electronics:pos_neg_small_margin_rate": 0.1482,
      "CDs_and_Vinyl:pos_neg_margin_p10": 2.9024,
      "CDs_and_Vinyl:pos_neg_neg_beats_pos_rate": 0.0132,
      "Electronics:embedding_collapse_score": 0.515
    },
    "brief_metric_read": {
      "Electronics:pos_neg_margin_p10": "Lower-tail separation is nearly zero.",
      "Electronics:pos_neg_small_margin_rate": "14.82% of sampled positions have weak separation.",
      "CDs_and_Vinyl:pos_neg_neg_beats_pos_rate": "Only 1.32% of sampled negatives outrank positives.",
      "Electronics:embedding_collapse_score": "Even the highest collapse score corresponds to mean cosine similarity of approximately 0.03."
    }
  }
}"}
